  "description": "The Music menu has an Album Artists item after Artists. It shows one entry for each Album Artist. All the songs of a compilation are under one entry, for example \"Various Artists\".",
  "details": [
    "Music > Album Artists shows the Album Artists in alphabetical order.",
    "A song without an Album Artist is under its Artist.",
    "Select an Album Artist to see its albums and songs.",
    "The Artists item and Now Playing do not change.",
    "Settings > Main Menu has an Album Artists row under Music. Set it to On to show Album Artists in the main menu."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The iPod reads the Album Artist when it reads the music database: at the start and after a sync.",
    "The Album Artists list has no letters for the fast scroll.",
    "The idea comes from osos-lab (RepriseOS) for the iPod Classic."
